diff --git a/scoping_notes.md b/scoping_notes.md
index abf9bd8..ebed19c 100755
--- a/scoping_notes.md
+++ b/scoping_notes.md
@@ -1,31 +1,20 @@
 Original scope
 
-- The official environment description calls for the full `helm-charts-editor` project layout,
-  the upstream `charts/mlflow` chart plus sibling chart directories, Helm and kubectl tooling,
-  and a lightweight Kubernetes cluster available for optional end-to-end validation.
+- The official environment description calls for the full `helm-charts-editor` project layout, the upstream `charts/mlflow` chart plus sibling chart directories, Helm and kubectl tooling, and a lightweight Kubernetes cluster available for optional end-to-end validation.
 
 Reduced scope used in this bundle
 
-- The bundle preserves the Linux `/app/helm-charts-editor` workspace shape, the target
-  `charts/mlflow` chart, sibling chart directory names, and the core Helm debugging surface.
-- `helm`, `kubectl`, and `kind` are installed, but the verifier uses `helm lint` and
-  `helm template` instead of requiring a pre-running nested cluster.
-- The sibling charts are kept as placeholders rather than full upstream copies because they are not
-  part of the capability target for this task.
-- The packaged chart archives and extra versioned directories from the original Windows seed are
-  omitted; they do not affect the PVC naming capability being evaluated.
+- The bundle preserves the Linux `/app/helm-charts-editor` workspace shape, the target `charts/mlflow` chart, sibling chart directory names, and the core Helm debugging surface.
+- `helm`, `kubectl`, and `kind` are installed, but the verifier uses `helm lint` and `helm template` instead of requiring a pre-running nested cluster.
+- The sibling charts are kept as placeholders rather than full upstream copies because they are not part of the capability target for this task.
+- The packaged chart archives and extra versioned directories from the original Windows seed are omitted; they do not affect the PVC naming capability being evaluated.
 
 Why this reduction is necessary
 
-- Public network access is unavailable in this construction environment, so the upstream
-  `community-charts/helm-charts` repository cannot be vendored faithfully into the bundle.
-- Requiring a fully running nested Kubernetes cluster would add substantial environment fragility
-  unrelated to the actual multi-file Helm naming task, especially in batch-mode static generation.
+- Public network access is unavailable in this construction environment, so the upstream `community-charts/helm-charts` repository cannot be vendored faithfully into the bundle.
+- Requiring a fully running nested Kubernetes cluster would add substantial environment fragility unrelated to the actual multi-file Helm naming task, especially in batch-mode static generation.
 
 Why the reduced task still preserves the capability target
 
-- The hard part remains the same: the solver must debug a realistic Helm chart across
-  `values.yaml`, `values.schema.json`, `templates/pvc.yaml`, and `templates/deployment.yaml`,
-  while navigating duplicate `persistence` schema blocks.
-- The verifier still checks rendered PVC identity, release-namespace placement, workload claim
-  usage, and file-level cleanup of stale release-name-only naming references.
+- The hard part remains the same: the solver must debug a realistic Helm chart across `values.yaml`, `values.schema.json`, `templates/pvc.yaml`, and `templates/deployment.yaml`, while navigating duplicate `persistence` schema blocks.
+- The verifier still checks rendered PVC identity, release-namespace placement, workload claim usage, and file-level cleanup of stale release-name-only naming references.
